a1908" :question/math-academy-id "q-116475" :question/problem "If $g(x)={\\int }_{0}^{x}{t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t$ for $x>0,$ determine ${g}^{′}(2).$" :question/worked-solution "The function ${t}^{2}{e}^{t}$ is continuous on $[0,x],$ where $x>0.$ So, FTC II applies, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{t}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={x}^{2}{e}^{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the value of ${g}^{′}(2),$ we substitute $x=2$ in the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}^{′}(2) & ={2}^{2}\\cdot {e}^{2} \\\\  & =4{e}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-116475/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "cf94b5cf-6407-5931-92df-9f87818e8a71"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-116475"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-30627/selection/3d67a4af70090573669da8b3e1434eb57e41c9115401332463078e750d5288b6" :answer/id #uuid "f69e7616-6f5b-552d-9533-ee47d2b14ff7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30627/selection/0428a2d6f7eeb8fed2485d7eb89a316e793a2ae9c0d87b06e62a59e24eab44b2" :answer/id #uuid "9e350179-f6ce-543f-bf52-0d1f02eb6646" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3{x}^{3}+b{x}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30627/selection/ecc243622739f75b62f1bea148049721f01078be9e7e354809ab6c4359e4e223" :answer/id #uuid "7b58277e-ae12-5d1b-becd-8434c1cf8aed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a{x}^{3}+b{x}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30627/selection/1dcc24733040f163f8d8719a2924ed1f5dba50bbbf6fb8971d5132d3818bf064" :answer/id #uuid "a4d8b4a0-d0ce-5544-846e-23a9dfe403f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "a{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-30627/selection/2b87de7d247f73455ec80c311f2a85adb00ec9a4abfbe28d9ecd9d41c5287a75" :answer/id #uuid "99d2a0